{
  "info": {
    "name": "NEOCOM Industry Blueprints",
    "description": "Manual checks for the async industry blueprint list (BASSE).\n\n- `GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}/industry/blueprints` — HTTP list (partial/stale OK; enrichment continues in background).\n- `GET /v1/pilots/{pilotId}/industry/blueprints/events` — SSE stream (`text/event-stream`); events type `node-updated` with `{ nodeId, node }`.\n\nUse environment **NEOCOM local** (`baseUrl`, `pilotId`). Server: `npm run start:dev` in `neocom-back`. Persistence/Redis optional (`.env.async` + `npm run docker:up`); without them Nest uses in-memory store and in-process enrichment.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "pilotId",
      "value": "93813310"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "List blueprints (first / persistence miss)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}/industry/blueprints",
        "description": "On persistence miss, Nest returns a simplified/partial list and starts background enrichment. Scaffold rows use `ready: false` and null calculated fields until enrichment finishes."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('returns a non-empty array', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(body.length).to.be.above(0);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('items are ProcessedBlueprint-shaped', function () {",
              "    body.forEach(function (row) {",
              "        pm.expect(row.jsonClass).to.eql('ProcessedBlueprint');",
              "        pm.expect(row.blueprintId).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(row.name).to.be.a('string');",
              "        pm.expect(row).to.have.property('ready');",
              "        pm.expect(row).to.have.property('manufactureIndex');",
              "        pm.expect(row).to.have.property('marketCost');",
              "        pm.expect(row).to.have.property('manufactureCost');",
              "    });",
              "});",
              "if (body.length) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('sampleBlueprintId', String(body[0].blueprintId));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List blueprints (second / persistence hit)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}/industry/blueprints",
        "description": "Repeat the list call. Should return persistence for the same pilot scope without requiring ESI again. After enrichment has run, some or all rows may show `ready: true` and filled calculated fields."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('returns a non-empty array', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(body.length).to.be.above(0);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('same scaffold blueprint ids still present', function () {",
              "    const ids = body.map(function (r) { return r.blueprintId; });",
              "    pm.expect(ids).to.include(1001);",
              "    pm.expect(ids).to.include(1002);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List blueprints — invalid pilotId",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/not-a-number/industry/blueprints",
        "description": "ParseIntPipe rejects a non-integer pilotId (typically 400)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 400', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SSE enrichment events",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "text/event-stream"
          },
          {
            "key": "Cache-Control",
            "value": "no-cache"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}/industry/blueprints/events",
        "description": "Opens the Nest `@Sse()` stream for this pilot industry scope.\n\n**How to use:** Send this request first (leave it open if your Postman supports event streams), then run **List blueprints** in another tab so enrichment can publish `node-updated` events.\n\nEvent payload shape: `event: node-updated` with data `{\"nodeId\":\"…\",\"node\":{…}}`.\n\nClassic Postman may treat this as a long-lived response; Postman v10+ Event Stream / Newman may differ. curl alternative:\n`curl -N -H 'Accept: text/event-stream' '{{baseUrl}}/v1/pilots/{{pilotId}}/industry/blueprints/events'`"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Readiness (sanity)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ready",
        "description": "Confirms the Nest process is up and reports version / environment / logLevel."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('ready report shape', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ready');",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('version');",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('environment');",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('logLevel');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
